        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-11-03T17:45:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>All the talk during the opening bit about 'stacks' confused me. At first, I thought they were talking smokestacks, but I'm thinking... soil stacks? I've never heard anyone refer to that as a \"main stack' though. Is this a St. Louis thing? c.c</p>\n<p>Happy birthday, Freya. :D And happy Christopher Time to us all. XD</p>\n<p>Apex the Wolf King is now my favorite Sentinels villain. XD This is great.</p>\n<p>All right, but hear me out: Laser Claus could be the name of a great Guise ally/villain. Think about it: Alien dude shows up in his rad cosmic sleigh, going, \"Joseph King! Space Christmas is in danger, you must help me save it!\" And Guise is all, \"Whoa, whoa, whoa, are you some kind of Santa Claus? Only&nbsp;<em>I</em>&nbsp;get to be Santa Claus.\" And he's like, \"No, it's cool, just put on your Santa costume and come help me bring joy and presents to all the good children of the galaxy.\" but Guise is just&nbsp;<em>livid</em>&nbsp;and swears a blood oath of vengeance or whatever it is Guise does because no one else gets to be Santa but him. It could happen!</p>\n<p>I hear what C&amp;A are saying, but in the Animalverse, Setbark <em>would</em> be a puppy, so...</p>\n<p>(Or is he Marmosetback?)</p>\n<p>If there's an awards show this year, Angry Taxpayer gets my vote for funniest letter for \"Have a nice bum, ya days.\" What a perfect episode for that joke to end up in, too. :D</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:10:07.514Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
